OWED: `{{ v:d:8 }}` on a positive i64 is space-padded with no plus (`   14683`).

Never green on the 2026-08-26..09-07 boards. Parked so the failed
column means regression again. Driven by --todo-sweep; drop this
marker when the pin is promotable.


---

RULED 2026-10-24: Koru owns the `:d:N` width semantic — space-pad, sign
only when negative (the oracle shape every external benchmark expects).
Raw-Zig passthrough ends at the interpolation spec: C# and JS are separate
emission targets, so a spec passed verbatim into Zig's format string makes
every backend inherit (or re-correct) a Zig 0.15 quirk. The `+` on
width-formatted positive signed ints is a host leak, not a surface.

Still owed: the lowering itself — the interpolation emitter needs a Koru
padding rule for `:d:N`. This pin stays red on `output` until it lands;
the ruling only decides WHERE the semantic lives. Named by the new
challenge `029_the_host_leak_audit` as its first exhibit.
